An argument that names something in a zk2 key — a service address, an
interface, a fingerprint — is a name the grammar has to be able to spell.
Typed at a shell, an illegal one is a usage error: exit 2, naming the argument
and the rule, before any session is opened (#509, kept through #612). That is
why none of these needs a bus. The list is every verb that takes one; a new
one belongs here.

v1's chunk positions (a producer, a config resource or group, refused by
`zenkey::grammar::is_valid_plain_chunk`) left with the verbs that took them —
`config`, `blob list` and `check conform` (#612, FJ9).

`check probe` and `check schema` name an interface since FJ8b (#612): the
name is zk2's `<name>.v<major>`, refused by the parser like any other.

```console
$ zenctl check probe host-a/tc MyApp namespaces
? 2
error: invalid value 'MyApp' for '<IFACE[@FP]>': interface "MyApp" is not <name>.v<major> with name segments [a-z][a-z0-9_]* (e.g. `tc.netif.v1`)

For more information, try '--help'.

```

```console
$ zenctl check probe host-a tc.netif.v1 namespaces
? 2
Error: host-a: binding "host-a" is not <system>/<service> (each a name or *)
check probe: the question could not be asked — exit 2, the reserved non-verdict (1 here would claim a verdict this run never reached)

```

```console
$ zenctl check schema MyApp namespaces --from '{}'
? 2
error: invalid value 'MyApp' for '<IFACE[@FP]>': interface "MyApp" is not <name>.v<major> with name segments [a-z][a-z0-9_]* (e.g. `tc.netif.v1`)

For more information, try '--help'.

```

zk2's names are refused at the same edge (#612, FJ4): a service address is
`<system>/<service>`, each a plain chunk, and an interface is
`<name>.v<major>`, optionally `@` a fingerprint or a prefix of one — lowercase
hex, `sha256:` optional. The model's own parsers decide, so the refusal is the
grammar's, not a second spelling of it.

```console
$ zenctl service show MyHost/tc
? 2
error: invalid value 'MyHost/tc' for '<SYSTEM/SERVICE>': system "MyHost" is not a plain chunk ([a-z0-9]([a-z0-9._-]*[a-z0-9])?)

For more information, try '--help'.

```

```console
$ zenctl service show host-a
? 2
error: invalid value 'host-a' for '<SYSTEM/SERVICE>': "host-a" is not a zk2 key: an address is <system>/<service>

For more information, try '--help'.

```

```console
$ zenctl iface show TcNetif
? 2
error: invalid value 'TcNetif' for '<IFACE[@FP]>': interface "TcNetif" is not <name>.v<major> with name segments [a-z][a-z0-9_]* (e.g. `tc.netif.v1`)

For more information, try '--help'.

```

```console
$ zenctl schema show tc.netif.v1@XYZ
? 2
error: invalid value 'tc.netif.v1@XYZ' for '<IFACE[@FP]>': "XYZ" is not a fingerprint: 1 to 64 lowercase hex digits, `sha256:` optional

For more information, try '--help'.

```

```console
$ zenctl service list --system Host-A --zenoh-config tests/cmd/fixtures/dead-bus.json5
? 2
Error: Host-A: system "Host-A" is not a plain chunk ([a-z0-9]([a-z0-9._-]*[a-z0-9])?)

```

`call`, `get state` and `watch` (FJ5) take the same address. `get state`'s
is one service, parsed at the edge; `call` and `watch` take a pattern too
(`*/tc`), so theirs is checked as R1's binding syntax, before a session:

```console
$ zenctl get state MyHost/tc tc.netif.v1 namespaces
? 2
error: invalid value 'MyHost/tc' for '<SYSTEM/SERVICE>': system "MyHost" is not a plain chunk ([a-z0-9]([a-z0-9._-]*[a-z0-9])?)

For more information, try '--help'.

```

```console
$ zenctl call MyHost/tc tc.netif.v1 diagnostics --zenoh-config tests/cmd/fixtures/dead-bus.json5
? 2
Error: MyHost/tc: binding "MyHost/tc" is not <system>/<service> (each a name or *)

```

```console
$ zenctl watch 'host-a/*/x' tc.netif.v1 'bandwidth/{ns}/{iface}' --zenoh-config tests/cmd/fixtures/dead-bus.json5
? 2
Error: host-a/*/x: binding "host-a/*/x" is not <system>/<service> (each a name or *)

```

The mock owners (FJ8a) take the same address: `gen` and `serve` run at one
service, parsed at the edge; `bench call` takes a pattern, as `call` does,
and so does a `--bind` provider.

```console
$ zenctl gen MyHost/tc
? 2
error: invalid value 'MyHost/tc' for '<SYSTEM/SERVICE>': system "MyHost" is not a plain chunk ([a-z0-9]([a-z0-9._-]*[a-z0-9])?)

For more information, try '--help'.

$ zenctl serve host-a tc.netif.v1 diagnostics
? 2
error: invalid value 'host-a' for '<SYSTEM/SERVICE>': "host-a" is not a zk2 key: an address is <system>/<service>

For more information, try '--help'.

$ zenctl bench call MyHost/tc tc.netif.v1 diagnostics --zenoh-config tests/cmd/fixtures/dead-bus.json5
? 2
Error: MyHost/tc: binding "MyHost/tc" is not <system>/<service> (each a name or *)

$ zenctl gen host-a/tc tc.netif.v1 --bind cmd=Host/x --dry-run
? 2
Error: Host/x: binding "Host/x" is not <system>/<service> (each a name or *)

```
